<h2>Per-client provisioning checklist</h2>

<p>Every new client touches these accounts. Checklist for the lead at kickoff:</p>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>GitHub repo created (private, named <code>pikes-peak-{client-slug}</code>)</li>
  <li>Cloudflare Pages project created + connected to repo</li>
  <li>Web3Forms access key generated + saved in <code>_data/site.js</code></li>
  <li>Drive folder created with sub-folders (assets, agreements, invoices, communications)</li>
  <li>UptimeRobot monitor added (waits until launch to enable)</li>
  <li>Domain added to WHOIS-watch list</li>
  <li>Stripe customer created + card-on-file (or ACH preference noted)</li>
  <li>Quickbooks customer created</li>
  <li>Active-clients spreadsheet row added (start date, plan, billing day, contact)</li>
</ul>

<h2>Per-client deprovisioning checklist (offboarding)</h2>

<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>GitHub repo archived (don't delete; private archive)</li>
  <li>Cloudflare Pages project deleted (after DNS pointed away)</li>
  <li>Web3Forms account ownership transferred to client</li>
  <li>Drive folder moved to <code>archive/{client}</code></li>
  <li>UptimeRobot monitor stopped</li>
  <li>Domain removed from WHOIS-watch list</li>
  <li>Stripe subscription canceled (after final invoice paid)</li>
  <li>Quickbooks customer marked inactive</li>
  <li>Removed from active-clients spreadsheet; added to former-clients with end date</li>
</ul>

<h2>Rotating credentials</h2>
<p>Twice a year (Jan + Jul), audit:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Stripe API keys</li>
  <li>Web3Forms access keys (rotate per client; update in their <code>_data/site.js</code> + redeploy)</li>
  <li>GitHub personal access tokens</li>
  <li>Cloudflare API tokens</li>
  <li>SSH keys (rotate annually)</li>
</ul>
<p>If a credential is suspected compromised: rotate same day. Don't wait for the schedule.</p>

