<h2>Hardware checklist for the operator's machine</h2>
<p>The single laptop the agency runs on is itself part of the security perimeter. Run this audit quarterly.</p>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>Full-disk encryption enabled (FileVault on Mac, BitLocker on Windows)</li>
  <li>OS auto-update enabled; current major version installed</li>
  <li>Password manager browser extension installed and signed in</li>
  <li>2FA hardware key (YubiKey) physically present; backup key stored in a separate location</li>
  <li>Time Machine / equivalent local backup running on a daily schedule to an encrypted external drive</li>
  <li>Cloud backup for the working directory (e.g., Backblaze) configured and verified</li>
  <li>Recovery codes for 1Password, GitHub, Cloudflare, registrar printed and stored in fireproof box</li>
  <li>Firewall enabled; no inbound services running unless explicitly required</li>
  <li>Browser running with reasonable privacy defaults (uBlock Origin, HTTPS-only mode, third-party cookies blocked)</li>
  <li>Old credentials and SSH keys cleaned up (every 6 months)</li>
  <li>Lock-screen timeout set to 5 minutes max; lock when stepping away</li>
  <li>If laptop is lost or stolen: documented response in /sop/checklists/ "Security incident response"</li>
</ul>

<h2>Read-only auditor access</h2>
<p>For accountants, lawyers, prospective acquirers, or insurance auditors who legitimately need to look but not touch.</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scoped Drive folder.</strong> A single folder at <code>/Operations/Audits/{auditor-name}/</code> with read-only permission. Anything they need lives there; they have no access to anything else.</li>
  <li><strong>Financials view.</strong> Read access to a specific Stripe export folder and the books export folder. Never live access to Stripe or the books platform.</li>
  <li><strong>Time-boxed.</strong> Auditor access is granted with an expiry date; calendar reminder set for the day after expiry to revoke.</li>
  <li><strong>No production access.</strong> Auditors do not get access to client repos, client analytics, client credentials, or anything that touches active client work.</li>
  <li><strong>NDA before access.</strong> Standard auditor NDA signed via DocuSign; archived alongside the audit.</li>
  <li><strong>Documented.</strong> Each audit has a one-page record: who, what was reviewed, what was found, dates of access. Filed in <code>/Operations/Audits/{auditor-name}/log.md</code>.</li>
</ul>
